<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prince Rupert of the Rhine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1619">1619</a>–<a href="/years/1682">1682</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prince Rupert of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> was a nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-england">Charles I of England</a>, a Royalist cavalry commander in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-civil-war">English Civil War</a> and later an admiral. A leading backer of the fur-trading voyages to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-bay">Hudson Bay</a>, he became the first governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudsons-bay-company">Hudson's Bay Company</a> when it was chartered in 1670, and the company's vast territory was named Rupert's Land after him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prince-rupert-of-the-rhine.jpg" alt="Prince Rupert of the Rhine" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter Lely · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_Lely_-_Prince_Rupert_of_the_Rhine_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
